            "CVE-2026-123367": {
                "cve_id": "CVE-2026-123367",
                "title": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphi ...",
                "description": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphics engine. Prior to 1.1.2, the bundled jpgd JPEG decoder accepts duplicate component selectors in an SOS scan header, causing each duplicate to increase m_blocks_per_mcu without checking the buffers sized from the frame components. A crafted grayscale JPEG can repeat its component in the SOS header, causing decode paths in src/loaders/jpg/tvgJpgd.cpp to write beyond heap buffers sized for one component. The issue is reachable through direct JPEG decoding and through JPEG images embedded in Lottie content, and confirmed impact is memory corruption followed by a process crash. This issue is fixed in version 1.1.2.",
                "severity": "HIGH",
                "status": "fixed",
                "events": [
                    {
                        "introduced": "0.15.13-2.fc43",
                        "identifier": "fc43",
                        "fixed": "1.0.6-2.fc43"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "CVE-2026-45729": {
                "cve_id": "CVE-2026-45729",
                "title": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphi ...",
                "description": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphics engine. Prior to version 1.0.5, a null pointer dereference in SvgLoader::run() allows any caller that passes untrusted SVG data to Picture::load() to crash the process with a 6-byte payload. This issue has been patched in version 1.0.5.",
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "status": "fixed",
                "events": [
                    {
                        "introduced": "0.15.13-2.fc43",
                        "identifier": "fc43",
                        "fixed": "1.0.6-1.fc43"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "CVE-2026-58496": {
                "cve_id": "CVE-2026-58496",
                "title": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphi ...",
                "description": "Thor Vector Graphics (ThorVG) is a production-ready vector graphics engine. Prior to 1.0.7, the `SFNT/TTF` font loader's `SfntLoader::gen` function in `tvgSfntLoader.cpp` reads `data[0] through data[3]` to identify the font type without first checking that the input buffer contains at least four bytes. Loading an undersized font directly from memory through public APIs such as `tvg::Text::load` causes an out-of-bounds read. Loading through a file path using `mmap` can mask the read because of page alignment; the memory-loading API directly exposes it. Depending on memory layout, a malformed short font may crash the consuming application or disclose adjacent heap memory. This issue is fixed in version 1.0.7.",
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "status": "fixed",
                "events": [
                    {
                        "introduced": "0.15.13-2.fc43",
                        "identifier": "fc43",
                        "fixed": "1.0.6-2.fc43"
                    }
                ]
            },
